\begin{proof}
Fix any distance weight $w \colon [0,\infty] \to [0,1]$.
If $M$ has a boundary, then fix an extension $M'$ of $M$, which is an open manifold containing $M$ in the interior. 
By $w^{-1}(0) = \{ 0 \}$, by definitions of $\delta$ and $\varepsilon_w$, we have $\varepsilon_w^{-1}(0) = \delta^{-1}(0) = \mathop{\mathrm{Sing}}(\F)$, which implies assertion (1).
From definition of $\varepsilon_w$, assertions (2) and (3) hold. 


