\begin{definition}
An isolated singular point outside of $\partial S$ is a $\bm{1}$-{\bf prong} (or {\bf thorn}) if the lift of some neighborhood $C$ of the singular point by $C \ni z\mapsto z^2 $ is a neighborhood of a $2$-prong. 
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}
An isolated singular point outside of $\partial S$ is a $\bm{0}$-{\bf prong} if it is a center. 
\end{definition}


