\begin{definition}
A prong connection $C$ is {\bf $f$-unstable} if it contains exactly one fake prong, any prongs except the fake prong in $C$ are $1$-prongs and $3$-prongs, $n_{V_-}(C) = b_1(C)$, and $D(\F) \cap \partial M = \emptyset$. 
\end{definition}


\begin{definition}
A prong connection $C$ is {\bf $p$-unstable} if $\mathrm{coheight}_{\mathrm{p,\F}}(C) = 2$, $n_{V_-}(C) + 1 = b_1(C)$, and $D(\F) \cap \partial M = \emptyset$, see Figure~\ref{p_unstable_prong_connection}.
