\label{disk_3prongs}
\end{figure}
%
For any convergence sequence $(\theta_n)$ of real numbers to $\theta_\infty \in \R$, the sequence $(\F(\theta_n))$ of regular foliations converges to the foliation $\F(\theta_\infty)$. 
This implies that the divergence-free regular foliation $\F(\theta)$ on the sphere $\mathbb{S}^2$ for any $\theta \in \R$ is not structurally stable. 


}
