\title{Mixed dynamics from the classical and quantum ergodic hierarchy}
\author{\textsc{Ignacio S. Gomez}$^{1}$ and \textsc{Federico H. Holik}$^{2}$}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
Based on the classical and quantum ergodic hierarchy, a framework for mixed systems with a phase space composed by two uncorrelated integrable and chaotic regions is presented. It provides some features of mixed systems connecting the intuitive notion of a mixed phase space with the mixing level of the ergodic hierarchy. The formalism is illustrated with the kicked rotator.\end{abstract}

