\end{figure}

We next introduce the energy functional
%As later, we will obtain our discretized linear system from the corresponding energy functional, we provide 
\begin{align}\label{eq:functional}
    J(u):=\int_{\Omega}\frac{1}{2}\alpha|\nabla u|^2+\frac{1}{2}\beta u^2-fu \, \d(x,y),
\end{align}
from which we obtain a symmetric linear system after a finite difference discretization as described further below.
We note that the weak formulation of problem~\eqref{eq:poisson} is equivalent to the minimization of the energy functional $J(u)$ in~\eqref{eq:functional} over a suitable Sobolev space, prescribing the boundary conditions $u_D$.

