\section{Background}\label{back}
% \setlength{\parskip} {-0.5pt}

% FSL definition 
% updated by hector
\textbf{Few-shot learning}. FSL can be formally defined as a machine learning problem where a model must quickly adapt to a new task using only a few training examples or ``shots'' per class \cite{ravi2017optimization}. Typically, FSL involves a ``meta-learning'' phase, where the model learns how to learn across a variety of tasks, and an ``adaptation'' phase, where it applies this knowledge to a previously unseen task with limited data.

% \textbf{Graph}. Graphs are fundamental data structures that model relationships and interactions between entities in various domains, including social networks, biological systems, and communication infrastructures. 
