\caption{Plot of the distance $\delta$ travelled by a ping-pong ball as a function of time. Triangles are used to indicate data from  a packing with a free surface; these data are a repeat of Fig.~\ref{resover}. The circles indicate a packing with a lid. The buoyancy stress is $\sigma_S \sim 210$~Pa for cases both with a free surface and with a solid lid on the top of the sample. Error bars indicate a 5\% error due to imaging resolution limitations. The sublinear dependence of distance with time is clear in the case when a lid is present. The insets have the same axes, are in double logarithmic scale, use the same symbols and highlight (a) the constant speed $\delta\propto t$ motion and (b) the sublinear power law behavior $\delta\propto t^{0.73}$ as best fits to the data.}
