\subsection{Operators: $O$}\label{sec:operators}

All operators are constant having conventional meanings as formally defined in Metamath database \texttt{set.mm} \cite{set.mm}.

\subsection{Infinitesimal Duration $\delta$}

Often, a tiny bit of time is useful for modeling.

\begin{definition}
Infinitesimal Duration $\delta$ is

\[ \delta \equiv \lim_{\tau \to 0} \tau
\] 
\end{definition}

Therefore, $(\tau \prec \tau + \delta)$.  Using $\tau'$ as shorthand for $\tau + \delta$, then $(\tau \prec \tau')$.



