\caption{The upper part of the figure depicts the inclusion relations between the different subclasses of QC-QCs considered in this paper (including the subclasses of QC-CCs, already presented in Fig.~\ref{fig:QCCC-classes}). For $N\ge 4$ (and nontrivial input and output spaces for the different parties) the inclusions between \textup{\textsf{QC-supFO}}, \textup{\textsf{QC-NIQC}} and \textup{\textsf{QC-QC}} are strict; for $N\le3$, \textup{\textsf{QC-NIQC}} reduces to \textup{\textsf{QC-supFO}}. It remains an open question whether the intersections with question marks are empty or not. \\
