	A representation $\rho$ as in the statement has to satisfy $\rho(\gamma_1)=M$ and $\rho(\gamma_2)=M^{-1}$, so that a $\mc P$-good $\rho$ is completely determined by $A\coloneqq \rho(\alpha)$ and $B \coloneqq \rho(\beta)$, with the following conditions:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item $A,B \in \SL_2(\mc O_K)$ and $ABA^{-1}B^{-1}=I$;
		\item $\tr A, \tr M^{-1}A \notin E$;
		\item The condition of \eqref{equation:numerical-condition-irreducibility} holds for $\tr A, \tr(M^{-1}A)$ and $\tr M$.
