\subsection{Studies on Simulated Missing-Modality Scenarios}
To further evaluate the impact of missing modalities, we use a publicly available simulated multiomics cancer dataset generated by the InterSim CRAN package, consisting of 500 samples across 15 clusters of varying sizes, reflecting realistic clinical scenarios. The dataset includes three omics modalities: DNA methylation, mRNA expression, and protein expression. The data is available on Zenodo \cite{ma_2024_13989262}, and further details about the data generation process can be found in the original publication \cite{ma2025moving}.

