		We are given the fact that $P^{(\mathfrak{a})}_{(\mu,i,i_1,i_2)} = 0 = P^{(\mathfrak{a})}_{(\nu,i,i_1,i_2)}$ which implies . Therefore,  for all $i,i_1,i_2, \in \{1,2,\ldots,n\}$ we have 
		\begin{equation} \label{freeOperad_eqn_univ_poly_rel_P2}
			\sum_{u=1}^n \alpha^u_{\gamma_2(\mu),i_1,i_2} X_{iu} 
			~=
			\sum_{s_1,s_2=1}^n 
			\alpha^i_{\gamma_2(\mu),s_1,s_2} X_{s_1i_1} X_{s_2i_2} \quad \text{and} \quad
			\sum_{u=1}^n \alpha^u_{\gamma_2(\nu),i_1,i_2} X_{iu} 
			~=
			\sum_{s_1,s_2=1}^n 
			\alpha^i_{\gamma_2(\nu),s_1,s_2} X_{s_1i_1} X_{s_2i_2} 
		\end{equation} 	
		We aim to show that the following equality holds: 
		\begin{equation*}
