\subsection{Storage and Memory Requirements}\label{sec:storage}

Storage is an essential part of any HPC infrastructure, just as important as CPU and GPU compute. If storage arrays fill up, new HPC jobs can't run, and existing jobs risk failure or data corruption. The increase in computing power from new HPC systems will be accompanied by a proportional increase in the amount of storage space required. Table \ref{tab:storage} shows the storage required for a day's worth of MD simulations running on a single HPC node, for different levels of performance.\\

